From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:21:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: give the A53 OPPs their
 real switch time

The A53 OPP tables declare a 100 us clock latency. A frequency change on
this board costs far more: on the station, setting VPROC1 through the
DA9214's I2C write and read back took 336 us on average (up to 1.04 ms
over 2393 changes), and a PLL step took 70-120 us more.

schedutil limits its updates to 1.5 times the transition latency, so
with 100 us it could re-pick a frequency about every 0.2 ms, faster than
a change completes. Declare 500 us, a typical voltage and clock change.
Its rate limit becomes about 0.8 ms.
